            <div xml:id="d594">

                <pb facs="0588" n="422" sameAs="frus:frus1917/pg422"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 337.11/350</note>
                <head ana="#head_untitled-inferred-from-preceding-sibling-head">[Untitled]</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-03-27T20:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 27, 1917, 8 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Cuba Company reports to Department 1,500 rebels visited Jobabo, Oriente Province
                    March 18, looting and destroying property, threatening destruction to mill.
                    American and British employees in danger. Have no reports since eighteenth.</p>
                <p>Investigate as to conditions at Jobabo, and advise Department what efforts Cuban
                    Government is making for protection there.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
